#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Bipartite graph of maximum degree 12 and diameter 5 on 12,960 vertices (thm-chartlift, Oct 24 2026): route-chart lift of the 4-regular base [[1,3],[3,1]] on 2+2 vertices over the metacyclic group Z_5 x|_2 Z_8 (order 40, m = 80), fibre F_3^4, 4 letters x 3 scalars; the chart r3/k4q3_diag_s126.txt (16 singular patterns, both diagonals covered) is one of the 348 labelled (4,3) diagonal charts. The base and group came from squad r3-chartlift card c1 (cost 4); the lead's alternation r3/alt348.sh (voltages <-> chart) closed it.
Self-contained (stdlib only).  Route-chart lift (CHART_LIFTS.md):
  * base: 4-regular bipartite multigraph on 2 + 2 vertices; base edge (a_i, b_j, colour c, voltage v);
  * controller: voltage lift by a group of order 40: (a_i, x) ~ (b_j, v * x); m = 80 vertices per side;
  * fibre F_3^4; controller edge of colour c lifts to ((a_i, x), u) ~ ((b_j, v*x), A_c u + lam b_c), lam in F_3.
Degree 4 x 3 = 12; order 2 * 80 * 81 = 12960.
F_3 elements are 0..2 with the tables below.  Vertex numbering: A-vertex ((a_i, x), u) -> (i*G + x)*81 + id(u);
B-vertex ((b_j, y), u) -> 6480 + (j*G + y)*81 + id(u); id(u) = sum u_t 3^t.
usage: python3 THIS out.edges   (apsp.c format: first line n, then one edge "u v" per line)"""
